1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:01,920
Twenty two miles of wall,

2
00:00:02,100 --> 00:00:03,730
built to trap one hill.

3
00:00:04,150 --> 00:00:07,970
In 52 BC, Julius Caesar cornered a Gallic army

4
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:10,230
on a hilltop town in eastern France.

5
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:12,520
He judged it too strong to storm.

6
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:14,710
So he ringed the hill instead:

7
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:15,780
a deep ditch,

8
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:17,840
a rampart about twelve feet high,

9
00:00:18,030 --> 00:00:20,370
and a wooden tower about every eighty feet.

10
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:23,850
Then Gallic riders slipped out at night to call for help.

11
00:00:24,030 --> 00:00:27,070
Caesar's answer was a second wall, facing outward,

12
00:00:27,220 --> 00:00:28,990
about thirteen miles around.

13
00:00:29,170 --> 00:00:31,720
His legions now sat between two rings.

14
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:34,230
In front of both, they buried traps:

15
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:36,050
rows of sharpened branches,

16
00:00:36,190 --> 00:00:37,620
hidden pits with stakes,

17
00:00:37,770 --> 00:00:39,450
and iron hooks set in wood.

18
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:41,120
When the relief army came,

19
00:00:41,210 --> 00:00:42,400
it hit the outer wall

20
00:00:42,450 --> 00:00:44,010
while the town hit the inner one,

21
00:00:44,170 --> 00:00:45,180
at the same time.

22
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:47,200
The lines bent, but held.

23
00:00:47,370 --> 00:00:49,630
Their leader, Vercingetorix, surrendered.

24
00:00:49,790 --> 00:00:53,130
All of it came down to twenty two miles of wall.
